{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells","id":978904,"title":"Flaming Sword and similar D&D spells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T00:43:18-07:00","id":978904,"title":"Flaming Sword and similar D&D spells","content":"A couple of times I have experienced that a player who is accustomed to D&amp;D-style magic wants to upgrade the damage of his weapon without knowing neither the Prime or Matter Arcana or the Adamant Hand Merit. Spells that temporarily imbue weapons with extra damage from fire, acid, cold and so on are a staple in that game. Specifically he wanted to put a damaging Death spell (Cold Snap, specifically) into his dagger so that it would release it's damage when hitting someone.<br /> I was not sure how to grant this; my reasoning was to let him cast Cold Snap on his weapon and let it release ONE time, as soon as he had caused damage with it. He thought this was disappointing while I pointed out that the original spell is only meant to be cast one at a time since they deal a lot of damage in a way that's not really parallell to how damage works in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> So, I was curious to know if the way I treated the situation was adequate or not. From reading the rules, it seems to me that the only way to produce high fantasy magic weapons is to either imbue them with Prime, enhance them with Matter or use the Adamant Hand Merit to unleash spells with an attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:58:32-07:00","id":978907,"title":"","content":"The next Mage 2e book is supposed to deal with things like one time use imbuements and the like without having to have Prime 4.<br /> <br /> But what you're describing - an item that can cast a spell - is an Imbued item. He can get one with merit dots or make it himself with Prime 4 + the appropriate Arcana for the spell.<br /> <br /> The Adamant Hand merit doesn't let you cast spells with an attack, it allows you to add an attack as a Yantra bonus to the next spell you cast.<br /> <br /> Having to &quot;buy&quot; or find a magic item you can't make yourself shouldn't be that strange for the player, after all that's what you do in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> I think that you handled the situation well as presented: it's always better to provide a minor compromise and keep the game moving than get into a protracted argument, but personally I'd let the player know that if he wants to have that magic item then he has to acquire it according to the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 09-30-2016, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:07:36-07:00","id":978910,"title":"","content":"The relative lack of elemental damage types kind of reduce the need for &quot;add a specific type of damage to an attack&quot; spells, but Creative Thaumaturgy should allow you to replicate the relevant Forces and Matter damage-boosting spells with other Arcana and/or special-effects-that-might-suggest-a-Reach-effect.<br /> <br /> Reskinning the Matter 3 &quot;Crucible&quot; spell to work with a different Arcanum can go a fair ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:11:51-07:00","id":978912,"title":"","content":"I guess you could use Forces to set the dagger on fire or make it very very cold. Mind you I can't see that making the weapon any more effective; and it's probably not going to be very good for the dagger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:53:07-07:00","id":979122,"title":"","content":"A Fate trigger to hold the spell until it meets the condition of striking. Your player would probably be interested in weapons made from the perfected metals previewed for Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:02:24-07:00","id":979128,"title":"","content":"I was wondering something about this earlier and I guess it can tie into this thread.<br /> <br /> There is a spell that allows you to turn a sling-stone into a boulder mid-shot. Maybe it's a magical item?<br /> <br /> Anyways, how would you do such a thing with, say, a gun or thrown item? Would it just be an Imbued Item with a Grow spell? And if so, how much more damage would it do? I imagine getting hit by a Size 5+ bullet is more or less like getting hit by a car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:17:45-07:00","id":979164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979128#post979128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering something about this earlier and I guess it can tie into this thread.<br /> <br /> There is a spell that allows you to turn a sling-stone into a boulder mid-shot. Maybe it's a magical item?<br /> <br /> Anyways, how would you do such a thing with, say, a gun or thrown item? Would it just be an Imbued Item with a Grow spell? And if so, how much more damage would it do? I imagine getting hit by a Size 5+ bullet is more or less like getting hit by a car.</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat it how you would getting hit by a car? I can't seem to recall the exact rules for that actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:19:31-07:00","id":979191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979164#post979164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Treat it how you would getting hit by a car? I can't seem to recall the exact rules for that actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would be the easy part. What about a bullet that is Size 2 or 3? Seems like you could just add +Size in Lethal, but a lump of metal the size of a dog traveling at 1700 miles per hour is probably going to hurt a bit more. Maybe 2x?<br /> <br /> Is the spell right? Would that work for an Imbued Item? Just a gun with Grow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:23:53-07:00","id":979235,"title":"","content":"Treat it like a cannon?<br /> <br /> That said, a Grow spell seems like it might work, though you might want to put a conditional trigger on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:11:26-07:00","id":979257,"title":"","content":"I guess it would slow down significantly because Grow does not increase the weight. 10 gram bullet with a size of a large dog. Have you ever tried to throw a large piece of styrofoam?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:23:31-07:00","id":979261,"title":"","content":"I think Grow or Shrink would change weights, it doesn't suggest that it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Either way the worst that would happen would be a slow down that resulted in less range, which wouldn't really matter unless you were sniping.<br /> <br /> Size in Chronicles 'is an abstract that reflects weight, mass, bulkiness and space.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:28:12-07:00","id":979262,"title":"","content":"I'd just make it an Artifact or Imbued Item that casts the desired damage spell when it strikes a living creature. Alternatively you could cast a relavent Forces spell that lights the weapon on fire or whatever using Hung Spell and maybe Condoitional Duration if you want to give it a trigger for when it activates.<br /> <br /> Also, just in general, Hung Spell and Conditional Duration are great for replicating Vancian-style prepared spells, in case you really want to make a D&amp;D Wizard in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:31:56-07:00","id":979263,"title":"","content":"It also doesn't suggest that it would gain more Durability. And it doesn't. <br /> <br /> Bullets &quot;work&quot; only because they are small and heavy for their size. You can't shoot with a ballon. <br /> <br /> Just throw some Reach on it to gain weight, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:34:28-07:00","id":979265,"title":"","content":"Disagree, Wonderous Machine is all about shooting with balloons. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:40:19-07:00","id":979268,"title":"","content":"Yeah. But its a different spell. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:15:47-07:00","id":979281,"title":"","content":"Durability depends on the material, the metal isn't changing so it would remain Durability 2 or 3, the same as a car.<br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying, but the mechanics of the real world don't seem to fit those of the Mage one on a 1:1 basis. You just get a six foot 'big' bullet.<br /> <br /> If you did have your balloon gun, though, you could use Alter Integrity to give those balloons the Durability of steel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:30:56-07:00","id":979318,"title":"","content":"Well, you can run a bunch of physics calculations and wind up with with an abomination of a spell that requires at least 3 different Arcana at 3+, or you can go with a Perfecting spell that adds its Potency to weapon damage. Your decision between realism and practicality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:38:30-07:00","id":979323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979318#post979318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or you can go with a Perfecting spell that adds its Potency to weapon damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if you can do that. You can add equipment bonuses to objects, but apparently that's not equivalent to weapon damage.<br /> <br /> Though there are easier ways to do damage, obviously, than using a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-30-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T01:59:49-07:00","id":979556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979323#post979323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure if you can do that. You can add equipment bonuses to objects, but apparently that's not equivalent to weapon damage.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that it's not in the listed spells doesn't mean you can't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:08:04-07:00","id":979566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979556#post979556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that it's not in the listed spells doesn't mean you can't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but the distinct lack of example spells which actually increase weapon damage suggests that just adding Potency to damage might be a bit heavy - very few spells add automatic <i>successes </i>- because of how powerful auto-successes are in the CoD system. I don't think that sort of spell is unreasonable, but I'd be tempted to give an effect like that Reach that it guaranteed a Paradox dice (i.e. a minimum of +3 for a 3-dot spell or +2 for a 4-dot spell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:01:37-07:00","id":979578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eggs Maledict</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979566#post979566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true, but the distinct lack of example spells which actually increase weapon damage suggests that just adding Potency to damage might be a bit heavy - very few spells add automatic <i>successes </i>- because of how powerful auto-successes are in the CoD system. I don't think that sort of spell is unreasonable, but I'd be tempted to give an effect like that Reach that it guaranteed a Paradox dice (i.e. a minimum of +3 for a 3-dot spell or +2 for a 4-dot spell).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember right Chronicles has a 1/3 sucessrate for dice, so what about adding 1/3 of the potency (round down min 1) to the damage, or full potency as dice to hit. Give him the option of picking one or the other and explain the benefits of both. 1/3 round down is the statistical average number of successes. Getting the extra dice means smiting things he couldn't tackle before, because their defenses were much higher. It turns your pocket knife into death's scythe.<br /> <br /> Also consider maybe allowing for reach for things like Armor Piercing, or reducing the number of successes needed to have a exceptional success, or ignoring supernatural powers that add armor or defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:12:59-07:00","id":979581,"title":"","content":"How is Knife +5 overpowered when the other one can just teleport you to the bottom of the ocean or make you kick yourself in the head or even stick this knife in you? I would go with half the potency rounded up and still wondering if I shouldnt just left if 1:1. Thyrsus can grant himself Stamina 1:1 which boosts his health 1:1 and its actually a similar case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:37:45-07:00","id":979589,"title":"","content":"Ice just flat-out can't do much in the brief amount of time it'd be making contact in a combat situation. The cold spells that I found all have effects over time, rather than instant.<br /> <br /> Flaming sword as per the thread title, though? Sure. Use your spell of choice to get the blade on fire, then just apply the damage as per the Size and Heat charts in the fire damage section.<br /> <br /> Same with electricity.<br /> <br /> Cold just isn't going to do any damage in a single turn unless you're shooting Icicles or maybe dealing with extreme sub-zero temperatures, but that cold and the dagger would likely become incredibly brittle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:34:19-07:00","id":979609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979589#post979589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ice just flat-out can't do much in the brief amount of time it'd be making contact in a combat situation. The cold spells that I found all have effects over time, rather than instant.<br /> <br /> Flaming sword as per the thread title, though? Sure. Use your spell of choice to get the blade on fire, then just apply the damage as per the Size and Heat charts in the fire damage section.<br /> <br /> Same with electricity.<br /> <br /> Cold just isn't going to do any damage in a single turn unless you're shooting Icicles or maybe dealing with extreme sub-zero temperatures, but that cold and the dagger would likely become incredibly brittle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> but I would argue for maybe just taking those bonus dice to the attack as after you add in the enemy defense something like that becomes pretty nice. I think the best defense I've seen outside a vampire with Celerity is 6, which can be some player characters entire attack pool or leave the combat beasts with just 2 to 3 dice. Getting potency dice means more success which means more damage.<br /> Though I question why the interest in more damage. Sounds like there might be something more going on we aren't seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:14:30-07:00","id":979790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979556#post979556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that it's not in the listed spells doesn't mean you can't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that.<br /> <br /> But when it comes down to it, a knife is a knife, and a sword is a sword. If you make that sword really fantastic you might get an advantage to its weapon damage, but as long as it's still a long, sharp blade, it's still going to stick to doing around the damage a long, sharp blade does. You might be able to enhance it so that it's like a 'chainblade,' with moving thorns that grind, but even then you're just basically making a souped up chainsaw, and you would stick to doing around the damage a chainsaw does. Providing the extent of your magic is 'making a weapon' you'll be doing around the level of damage that weapon does. If you want more, you'll have to add more and different magic to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-01-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:29:17-07:00","id":979823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979581#post979581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Knife +5 overpowered when the other one can just teleport you to the bottom of the ocean or make you kick yourself in the head or even stick this knife in you? I would go with half the potency rounded up and still wondering if I shouldnt just left if 1:1. Thyrsus can grant himself Stamina 1:1 which boosts his health 1:1 and its actually a similar case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, enhancing a weapons ability to do damage is pretty simple. It would obviously be a Perfecting spell, probably increase the weapon damage on a 1:1 basis, with a +1 Reach effect of allowing Potency to be spent on adding levels of armor penetration or the like. The only likely limitations might be that you can only add up to 5 weapon damage or something, maybe with another +1 Reach affect to go beyond that. All in all it's fairly straightforward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:17:56-07:00","id":980031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978904-flaming-sword-and-similar-d-d-spells?p=979581#post979581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Knife +5 overpowered when the other one can just teleport you to the bottom of the ocean or make you kick yourself in the head or even stick this knife in you? I would go with half the potency rounded up and still wondering if I shouldnt just left if 1:1. Thyrsus can grant himself Stamina 1:1 which boosts his health 1:1 and its actually a similar case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess there's a few things here.<br /> <br /> 1. Automatic successes (even if only applied after a successful roll) are much stronger than just adding dice.<br /> <br /> 2. You could stack +dice with +successes. <br /> <br /> 3. Adding Stamina would be the equivalent of a one-off hit buff, since one hit would strip the health right back off. The Stamina also doesn't add auto-successes when added to a pool. <br /> <br /> 4. The teleport spell would be Withstood, and need sympathy, which would increase the Withstand rating <br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is already a spell (Grave Misfortune) that increases damage if the target damage, to one particular subject. It's limited to that target, but also applies to ANY damage dealt. <br /> <br /> So...I forgot about Grave Misfortune previously. My bad. I'd probably be ok with it as a Fate spell, maybe a Death spell, or a Matter spell, or something else with a creative approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}